# What the Docker builds leave out of their context (ADR-0030). Every image is built from the root of the repository, so this keeps
# out what must never be in a layer (secrets, the history) and what is big or made by a build (installed packages, output), which the
# image makes again for itself.

# Secrets and history
.git
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Made by a build or installed by a package manager
**/node_modules
**/target
**/.cpcache
**/.shadow-cljs
design/dist

# Not part of any image
docs
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/.clj-kondo
**/.lsp
**/.calva
**/.nrepl-port
**/*.log
